---
// What it takes: one value stream, followed through the cycle in pencil, by
// the people who do the work. Every map drawn in these scenes follows one
// rule: a pale step is done by hand, a dark step runs on its own. The reader
// sees the balance hold through Declare, however much the map is argued over,
// and turn in Refactor. The sheet's legend states the rule once.
//
// Each stage is a demonstration the reader can run without us, set out the
// way a demonstration has always been set out: the premise they can check
// against their own organization; the reasoning, keyed to the position
// sheets it rests on; the one decision the stage fixes; its rules, each with
// its reason, as the sheet's notes; what it earns, as the conclusion; and
// the question their own reasoning asks next, as the way on. The last
// question returns to See, because the unit was one stream and there are
// others. Nothing is held back for a conversation.
//
// One DOM serves every reader. Without script the stages read in order as
// small multiples. With script the loop is the control at every width: beside
// the stage on wide screens, pinned above it on a phone, where a swipe also
// turns the stage.
import { Picture } from "astro:assets";
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import see from "../assets/consulting/see.jpg";
import declareMain from "../assets/consulting/declare-main.jpg";
import declare2 from "../assets/consulting/declare-2.jpg";
import declare3 from "../assets/consulting/declare-3.jpg";
import declare4 from "../assets/consulting/declare-4.jpg";
import declare5 from "../assets/consulting/declare-5.jpg";
import refactor from "../assets/consulting/refactor.jpg";
import proto1 from "../assets/consulting/proto-1.jpg";
import proto2 from "../assets/consulting/proto-2.jpg";
import proto3 from "../assets/consulting/proto-3.jpg";
import proto4 from "../assets/consulting/proto-4.jpg";
import scale from "../assets/consulting/scale.jpg";

// ---- the stages ------------------------------------------------------------
// In the reasoning, `{02}` keys the sentence to position sheet 02, and
// `*record*` marks the term where it is defined. One term per stage.
type Note = { rule: string; why: string };
const stages = [
  {
    id: "see",
    name: "See",
    premise:
      "The work a customer is owed crosses every department and belongs to none of them.",
    reason:
      "Each department writes down its own part.{01} The handoff between two departments belongs to neither, so neither writes it, and a person carries each case across it by judgment: the one who knows to call finance, the desk that settles the exception. A *stream* is the path those handoffs lie along, from the event that starts it, an order placed or a claim filed, to what the customer is owed at the end.",
    fixed: "Decided here: the two ends of the stream.",
    notes: [
      {
        rule: "Only the ends are fixed,",
        why: "because only they were written by someone outside: the order or claim that arrives, and the promise it is owed. Everything between is paper and judgment mixed, which the next stage separates.",
      },
      {
        rule: "Nothing is reorganized,",
        why: "because a reorganization moves departments, and the handoffs stay between whichever departments are now adjacent.",
      },
      {
        rule: "Choose the stream where customers wait,",
        why: "because waiting is a case sitting with someone who has to decide or ask,{04} and that stream holds the most judgment to write down.",
      },
    ],
    earns:
      "One stream, and the obligation at its end that everything after this is measured against.",
    next: "Whose version of it is true?",
    alt: "Four people around a small table as one of them draws the first line of a map.",
  },
  {
    id: "declare",
    name: "Declare",
    premise:
      "The people doing the work are the only ones who know how it runs, and they show it only when it’s safe to.",
    reason:
      "A rule on paper was written in advance by someone who did not see every case. A case is that rule completed by judgment at the moment it ran.{01} Ask for the rule and you get the advance version. Ask about a case, who decided, what they looked at, what they decided, and whether that matched the paper, and you get the judgment with it. Written from cases, that is the *record*.",
    fixed:
      "Decided here, before anyone is asked: the record of practice is the true one. The chart, the policy and the map become intentions.",
    notes: [
      {
        rule: "The decision comes first,",
        why: "because a workaround is a written rule a person overrode to get the work done, and whoever reports it is naming a rule they broke. Once the record is the truth, reporting a workaround records a rule instead of confessing to breaking one.",
      },
      {
        rule: "It is done when the people whose judgment it describes say it is theirs,",
        why: "not when it is signed, because a signature is a rule written by someone who did not see the cases, which is what the paper was.",
      },
      {
        rule: "Nothing is automated yet,",
        why: "because an agent built from the paper rule runs the advance version with the person who used to override it taken out of the loop, so the wrong rule now runs every time at the agent’s speed.",
      },
    ],
    earns:
      "For each decision on the stream: who makes it in practice, on which facts, from which system, and up to where. That is what agents will act on.",
    next: "What should it become?",
    alt: "A team argues over a value stream map on the wall; over later sessions the map fills with notes and redrawn lines.",
  },
  {
    id: "refactor",
    name: "Refactor",
    premise: "Automating one step of a tangled stream only tangles it faster.",
    reason:
      "The back-and-forth in a stream is judgment supplied in gaps: an approval is a person deciding where nothing written reached, and a relay is status moved by hand because no one could see it.{04} Speed one step and cases reach those gaps sooner, where the same person decides at the same pace, so the queue grows. The stream is redesigned whole, and every decision on it is given one holder within a *limit*, the amount or the condition past which it returns to a person.",
    fixed: "Decided here: who decides what, and up to where.",
    notes: [
      {
        rule: "A decision determined entirely by facts goes to software. One determined by facts within a range goes to an agent inside the limit and a person beyond it,",
        why: "because a limit is the one form of authority that can be handed over and taken back.{02} One that no one can yet write stays with a person.",
      },
      {
        rule: "Every term gets one definition,",
        why: "because a fact defined three ways was being chosen between by a person each time,{03} and every system is made to answer to the one.",
      },
      {
        rule: "Every role sees the design before it is built,",
        why: "because it moves decisions they hold, and they are the only people who can say whether what is written is the judgment they were using.",
      },
    ],
    earns:
      "The approvals that were only judgment in a gap are gone, the ones that remain are limits, and each limit is one line that says what to do and where to stop.",
    next: "Will it hold in operation?",
    alt: "A clean new map, most of its steps now dark, pinned alone on a sunlit wall.",
  },
  {
    id: "prototype",
    name: "Prototype",
    premise: "Every redesign looks right on the wall.",
    reason:
      "The redesign is a claim: these decisions, within these limits, on these definitions, handle the cases. It is new paper, and it will run twice until it has run once.{01} It *holds* when cases go through it with no gap needing a person, and the cases that count are the exceptions the record found, because those are where judgment used to be needed.",
    fixed:
      "Decided here: what counts as proof. Nothing scales until it has held live.",
    notes: [
      {
        rule: "Run it live, beside the old stream, on one case type or one region:",
        why: "live, because invented cases hold only the judgment their inventor already knew; beside, because the old stream still carries everything the slice does not; small, because the cost of a failed run is the judgment a person supplies afterward to repair it.",
      },
      {
        rule: "Build it from the record itself, not from a requirements document written from it,",
        why: "because a document written from the record is a second version, read by the builder instead of the first, and the two drift.{01} The builders work from the decision table, and the agents run it.",
      },
      {
        rule: "When a run fails, the fault is in the record:",
        why: "a limit set wrong, so the agent decided what a person should have or sent up what it could have decided,{02} or a definition still plural.{03} Write the fact and run again.",
      },
    ],
    earns:
      "A stream that has run through its exceptions, revised run by run by the people who will own it.",
    next: "What does it deliver at full load?",
    alt: "Engineers and business people building together, revising, laughing at a failed run, and watching it work.",
  },
  {
    id: "scale",
    name: "Scale",
    premise:
      "A pilot can succeed for a year without a single customer noticing.",
    reason:
      "A pilot handles a slice. Every other case still goes through the old stream, where judgment fills the gaps at the old pace, so for nearly every customer the wait is unchanged. The *load* is every case the stream receives, every day, exceptions included. The earlier stages exist so that the whole of it can move, because only then is judgment supplied nowhere but at the limits, where it is written.",
    fixed:
      "Decided here: what counts as done. The old stream is retired once the new one has carried the whole load through a round of its exceptions.",
    notes: [
      {
        rule: "The whole load, not a share,",
        why: "because while both streams run, people decide by hand which one a case belongs to and reconcile two records,{01} and the definitions drift apart again.{03}",
      },
      {
        rule: "Retiring the old stream is the sponsor’s decision,",
        why: "because it removes the fallback: after it, a failing case cannot be handed back to people informally and has to be met at a limit, and only the sponsor holds the authority the limits were cut from.",
      },
      {
        rule: "Measure what the customer gets:",
        why: "the time from the trigger to the obligation met, because waiting was judgment in a gap, and the share of cases completed without a person stepping in, because that is how much of the stream is now written.",
      },
    ],
    earns:
      "On that stream the managers stop approving, relaying and chasing, because those gaps no longer exist, and what they hold is the limits, which they set and revise.{04}",
    next: "Which stream is next?",
    alt: "The working floor of a healthy company: people settling things on the spot, deciding standing up, teaching one another; technology small and far back.",
  },
] as const satisfies readonly {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  premise: string;
  reason: string;
  fixed: string;
  notes: readonly Note[];
  earns: string;
  next: string;
  alt: string;
}[];

// ---- the keys: a sentence rests on a numbered sheet -------------------------
const sheets = new Map(
  (await getCollection("positions")).map(({ data }) => [
    String(data.sheet).padStart(2, "0"),
    data.short,
  ]),
);
const escape = (t: string) =>
  t.replace(/&/g, "&amp;").replace(/</g, "&lt;").replace(/>/g, "&gt;");
// `{02}` becomes a key to sheet 02; `*term*` marks the term where it is defined
const mark = (t: string) =>
  escape(t)
    .replace(/\{(\d\d)\}/g, (_, n) => {
      const short = sheets.get(n);
      if (!short) throw new Error(`no position sheet ${n}`);
      return `<a class="key" href="#position-${n}" aria-label="Sheet ${n}, ${escape(short)}" title="${escape(short)}">${n}</a>`;
    })
    .replace(/\*([^*]+)\*/g, "<dfn>$1</dfn>");
const f = (n: number) => n.toFixed(1);

// ---- the loop control ----------------------------------------------------
// five balloons on a circle, clockwise from the top; prototype carries its
// own small loop, because it turns until it holds
const R = 92;
const C = 120;
const loop = stages.map((s, i) => {
  const a = (-90 + i * 72) * (Math.PI / 180);
  return {
    ...s,
    x: C + R * Math.cos(a),
    y: C + R * Math.sin(a),
    // label sits outside the circle
    lx: C + (R + 30) * Math.cos(a),
    ly: C + (R + 30) * Math.sin(a),
    anchor: Math.cos(a) > 0.2 ? "start" : Math.cos(a) < -0.2 ? "end" : "middle",
  };
});
const innerR = 14;
const innerC = {
  x: C + (R - 34) * Math.cos((-90 + 3 * 72) * (Math.PI / 180)),
  y: C + (R - 34) * Math.sin((-90 + 3 * 72) * (Math.PI / 180)),
};
// the arrowhead that closes the loop, just before SEE; the small loop's
// head is the same mark at the same place on its own circle, smaller
const closeA = (-90 - 14) * (Math.PI / 180);
const close = { x: C + R * Math.cos(closeA), y: C + R * Math.sin(closeA) };
const innerClose = {
  x: innerC.x + innerR * Math.cos(closeA),
  y: innerC.y + innerR * Math.sin(closeA),
};
---

<div class="cycle" data-cycle>
  <div class="loop-band">
    <div class="loop">
      <svg class="loop-art" viewBox="0 0 240 240" aria-hidden="true">
        <circle class="loop-path" cx={C} cy={C} r={R}></circle>
        <path
          class="loop-head"
          d={`M ${f(close.x)} ${f(close.y)} l 7 -4 l -1 8 z`}
          transform={`rotate(-14 ${f(close.x)} ${f(close.y)})`}></path>
        <circle class="loop-inner" cx={f(innerC.x)} cy={f(innerC.y)} r={innerR}
        ></circle>
        <path
          class="loop-inner-head"
          d={`M ${f(innerClose.x)} ${f(innerClose.y)} l 5 -3 l -1 6 z`}
          transform={`rotate(-14 ${f(innerClose.x)} ${f(innerClose.y)})`}
        ></path>
      </svg>
      <div class="balloons" role="group" aria-label="Stages of the cycle">
        {
          loop.map((s, i) => (
            <button
              type="button"
              class="balloon"
              data-stage={s.id}
              aria-pressed={i === 0 ? "true" : "false"}
              style={`--x: ${f((s.x / 240) * 100)}%; --y: ${f((s.y / 240) * 100)}%; --lx: ${f((s.lx / 240) * 100)}%; --ly: ${f((s.ly / 240) * 100)}%`}
            >
              <span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">
                {String(i + 1).padStart(2, "0")}
              </span>
              <span class:list={["name", `anchor-${s.anchor}`]}>{s.name}</span>
            </button>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="states" data-states>
    {
      stages.map((s, i) => (
        <figure
          class:list={["state", `state-${s.id}`]}
          data-state={s.id}
          data-active={i === 0 ? "true" : "false"}
        >
          <div class="enunciation">
            <span class="mono-label">
              {String(i + 1).padStart(2, "0")} · {s.name}
            </span>
            <span class="premise">{s.premise}</span>
          </div>
          <div class="exhibit" role="img" aria-label={s.alt}>
            {s.id === "see" && (
              <Picture
                src={see}
                alt=""
                widths={[480, 960]}
                sizes="(max-width: 899px) 100vw, 30rem"
                formats={["avif", "webp"]}
                loading="lazy"
              />
            )}
            {s.id === "declare" && (
              <>
                <Picture
                  class="lead"
                  src={declareMain}
                  alt=""
                  widths={[540, 1080]}
                  sizes="(max-width: 899px) 100vw, 34rem"
                  formats={["avif", "webp"]}
                  loading="lazy"
                />
                <div class="sessions">
                  {[declare2, declare3, declare4, declare5].map((img) => (
                    <Picture
                      src={img}
                      alt=""
                      widths={[200, 400]}
                      sizes="(max-width: 899px) 50vw, 8rem"
                      formats={["avif", "webp"]}
                      loading="lazy"
                    />
                  ))}
                </div>
              </>
            )}
            {s.id === "refactor" && (
              <Picture
                src={refactor}
                alt=""
                widths={[640, 1280]}
                sizes="(max-width: 899px) 100vw, 40rem"
                formats={["avif", "webp"]}
                loading="lazy"
              />
            )}
            {s.id === "prototype" && (
              <div class="montage">
                {[proto1, proto2, proto3, proto4].map((img) => (
                  <Picture
                    src={img}
                    alt=""
                    widths={[200, 400]}
                    sizes="(max-width: 899px) 50vw, 11rem"
                    formats={["avif", "webp"]}
                    loading="lazy"
                  />
                ))}
              </div>
            )}
            {s.id === "scale" && (
              <Picture
                src={scale}
                alt=""
                widths={[720, 1440]}
                sizes="(max-width: 899px) 100vw, 60rem"
                formats={["avif", "webp"]}
                loading="lazy"
              />
            )}
          </div>
          <figcaption class="commentary">
            <p class="reason" set:html={mark(s.reason)} />
            <p class="fixed" set:html={mark(s.fixed)} />
            <ol class="notes" aria-label="Rules">
              {s.notes.map((n) => (
                <li>
                  <span class="rule" set:html={mark(n.rule)} />{" "}
                  <span class="why" set:html={mark(n.why)} />
                </li>
              ))}
            </ol>
            <p class="earns" set:html={mark(s.earns)} />
            <button
              type="button"
              class="next go"
              data-next={stages[(i + 1) % stages.length].id}
            >
              {s.next}
              <svg
                viewBox="0 0 12 12"
                width="0.62em"
                height="0.62em"
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
                <path
                  d="M2 6h8M6.5 2.5 10 6l-3.5 3.5"
                  fill="none"
                  stroke="currentColor"
                  stroke-width="1.1"
                  stroke-linecap="round"
                  stroke-linejoin="round"
                />
              </svg>
            </button>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      ))
    }
  </div>

  <p class="legend mono-label">
    <span class="swatch pale" aria-hidden="true"></span> by hand
    <span class="swatch dark" aria-hidden="true"></span> runs on its own
  </p>
</div>

<script is:inline>
  // the loop is the control. a stage is chosen from the loop (click, tap, or
  // arrow keys), by its own next question, or on a phone by a swipe; it
  // changes in place and enters from the side it was reached from. hover
  // previews a stage only where there is a pointer to hover with.
  (() => {
    const root = document.querySelector("[data-cycle]");
    if (!root) return;
    const hover = matchMedia("(hover: hover)");
    const narrow = matchMedia("(max-width: 899px)");
    const still = matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)");
    const buttons = [...root.querySelectorAll("[data-stage]")];
    const states = [...root.querySelectorAll("[data-state]")];
    const order = buttons.map((b) => b.dataset.stage);
    let selected = order[0];
    const visited = new Set();
    const show = (id) =>
      states.forEach(
        (s) => (s.dataset.active = String(s.dataset.state === id)),
      );
    const enter = (id, dir) => {
      if (!dir || still.matches) return;
      root.querySelector(`[data-state="${id}"]`)?.animate(
        [
          { opacity: 0, transform: `translateX(${dir * 24}px)` },
          { opacity: 1, transform: "none" },
        ],
        { duration: 380, easing: "cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.6, 0.2, 1)" },
      );
    };
    // the next stage is drawn in full ink: the way on. after Scale, See.
    const select = (id) => {
      const dir = Math.sign(order.indexOf(id) - order.indexOf(selected));
      selected = id;
      visited.add(id);
      const next = order[(order.indexOf(id) + 1) % order.length];
      buttons.forEach((b) => {
        const stage = b.dataset.stage;
        b.setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(stage === id));
        b.dataset.visited = String(visited.has(stage) && stage !== id);
        b.dataset.next = String(stage === next);
      });
      show(id);
      enter(id, dir);
    };
    // on a phone the loop is pinned above the stage; a new stage is brought
    // back up under it, so it is read from its top
    const settle = () => {
      if (!narrow.matches) return;
      const bar = document.querySelector(".bar")?.offsetHeight ?? 0;
      const top = root.getBoundingClientRect().top - bar;
      if (top < 0)
        scrollBy({ top, behavior: still.matches ? "auto" : "smooth" });
    };
    const step = (delta) => {
      const id = order[order.indexOf(selected) + delta];
      if (!id) return false;
      select(id);
      settle();
      return true;
    };
    root.querySelectorAll("[data-next]").forEach((n) =>
      n.addEventListener("click", () => {
        select(n.dataset.next);
        settle();
        root
          .querySelector(`[data-stage="${n.dataset.next}"]`)
          ?.focus({ preventScroll: true });
      }),
    );
    buttons.forEach((b) => {
      b.addEventListener("click", () => select(b.dataset.stage));
      b.addEventListener("mouseenter", () => {
        if (hover.matches) show(b.dataset.stage);
      });
      b.addEventListener("mouseleave", () => {
        if (hover.matches) show(selected);
      });
      b.addEventListener("focus", () => {
        if (b.dataset.stage !== selected) select(b.dataset.stage);
      });
      b.addEventListener("keydown", (e) => {
        const delta = {
          ArrowRight: 1,
          ArrowDown: 1,
          ArrowLeft: -1,
          ArrowUp: -1,
        }[e.key];
        if (!delta) return;
        e.preventDefault();
        if (step(delta))
          root
            .querySelector(`[data-stage="${selected}"]`)
            ?.focus({ preventScroll: true });
      });
    });
    // a sideways swipe across the stage turns it; a vertical one scrolls
    const field = root.querySelector("[data-states]");
    let from = null;
    field.addEventListener(
      "touchstart",
      (e) => (from = { x: e.touches[0].clientX, y: e.touches[0].clientY }),
      { passive: true },
    );
    field.addEventListener(
      "touchend",
      (e) => {
        if (!from) return;
        const dx = e.changedTouches[0].clientX - from.x;
        const dy = e.changedTouches[0].clientY - from.y;
        from = null;
        if (Math.abs(dx) > 48 && Math.abs(dx) > Math.abs(dy) * 1.5)
          step(dx < 0 ? 1 : -1);
      },
      { passive: true },
    );
    root.classList.add("interactive");
    select(selected);
  })();
</script>

<style>
  /* ---- the stage: enunciation across the top, then the plate and its
     commentary hanging from one edge, as a plate and its notes do in a
     folio. as small multiples (no script) every stage reads in order ---- */
  .states {
    display: grid;
    gap: 3rem;
  }
  .state {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    row-gap: 1.1rem;
  }
  .enunciation {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.45rem;
  }
  /* the premise: what the reader checks against their own organization */
  .premise {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 2vw, 1.7rem);
    line-height: 1.22;
    color: var(--ink);
    max-width: 34ch;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .commentary {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0;
    align-content: start;
    max-width: 34rem;
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.2vw, 1.08rem);
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--ink-light);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  /* the reasoning: keyed to the sheets it rests on */
  .reason {
    margin: 0;
  }
  /* the term, where it is defined */
  .commentary :global(dfn) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  /* a key to a position sheet, set like the sheet numbers in the index */
  .commentary :global(.key) {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-left: 0.3em;
    vertical-align: 0.42em;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.58em;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--ink-quiet);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-faint);
    transition:
      color 0.3s var(--ease),
      border-color 0.3s var(--ease);
  }
  .commentary :global(.key:hover),
  .commentary :global(.key:focus-visible) {
    color: var(--ink);
    border-color: var(--ink);
    outline: none;
  }
  /* the one decision this stage fixes: the middle reading speed, set as a
     claim under a hairline */
  .fixed {
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    padding-top: 0.85rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-faint);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 0.92em;
    line-height: 1.38;
    color: var(--ink);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  /* the rules, numbered as a sheet's general notes: the rule dark and
     short, its reason after it in the lighter face */
  .notes {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0.95rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    counter-reset: note;
  }
  .notes li {
    counter-increment: note;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.25rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    column-gap: 0.25rem;
    align-items: baseline;
    line-height: 1.42;
  }
  /* plain numerals: the two-digit form belongs to the sheets and their keys */
  .notes li::before {
    content: counter(note);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
